{"author":"RebarBotNava","author_email":"joeoakhart+bot@navapbc.com","author_id":"594c-9dcf-5ad6-4e6d","author_sig":"{\"payload\": \"\", \"payloadType\": \"application/vnd.rebar.authorship.v1+json\", \"signatures\": [{\"keyid\": \"594c-9dcf-5ad6-4e6d\", \"sig\": \"\"}]}","data":{"body":"rebar-debug Phase 2 held-out validation complete. The first hidden run exposed two oracle-fixture mistakes (isolated evidence calls were incorrectly forced to exhaust, contradicting the frozen precondition; freeform citations used the wrong public shape). Each correction was made in a separate clean origin/main worktree with the repair absent, and the final oracle was re-proven RED there (2 collected/2 expected failures) before being reapplied. The corrected held-out oracle then found one real incomplete fix: recovery returned a verdict, but exhausted recovery dropped trace/usage fields from the persisted sidecar. Root cause was `_bounded_diagnostic` pre-seeding fields with None and then using setdefault, plus not flattening nested exception.usage. The fixer added a persisted-event boundary test, proved RED, fixed the merge, ran an exact defect-seeded mutation back to RED, and restored GREEN. Final unchanged held-out run: 2 passed. Independent mutation check deleted the recovery dispatch and the held-out oracle returned 2 FAILED; restoring the dispatch returned 2 passed. Refactoring litmus passes: assertions are on public verdict, fail-closed error/sidecar, schema-valid criterion records, and fresh tool-free execution mode—not private helper names or intermediate variables."},"env_id":"ade0f2ef-51cc-45a2-bb97-c09846cd3df5","event_type":"COMMENT","timestamp":1785182143718589001,"uuid":"7e801955-a362-46e4-a6c1-657c1aebd9a4"}